;; WS-E generality sibling #2 — declared ownership map for the WAR MACHINE
;; belief path, the CURRENT implementation as described in
;; ~/code/p4ng/plop-2026.tex (glossary \srcref anchors). Authored by claude-7
;; (2026-08-15). Checked with repo-root /home/joe/code/futon2.
;;
;; Referent verification (the reason this map exists at all): the paper's War
;; Machine is the FUTON2 implementation — scheduled loop entry point
;; scripts/wm_scheduled_run.clj; belief path src/futon2/aif/belief.clj;
;; production seam scripts/futon2/report/war_machine.clj — NOT the futon3c
;; pilot peripheral. Mapping the pilot would have been the day's third
;; two-machines specimen; the operator's insistence on pinning the referent
;; prevented it.
;;
;; Scope: the A/B/D model-manifest seam the paper describes ("each trace
;; stamps the selected likelihood mode and content hashes for A, B, and D").
;; Deliberate declaration: the three content hashes are consumed at src
;; grain only by the paper-cited live-wiring test — provenance stamps are
;; write-mostly BY DESIGN (they exist for later audit, like flight
;; evidence-refs); the test is the reader that makes them load-bearing.
;; This sibling also exercises the checker on a machine that does NOT run
;; on the futon3c cycle engine and lives in a different repo: no :phases
;; section, spec-model generality only.
;;
;; CORRECTED 2026-09-25 (claude-11, DIAGRAMPROVER-WIRING-I2): the mode's
;; direction was declared backwards. At futon2 e1f6d909 war_machine.clj
;; decides it (arena-likelihood-mode, :818) and writes it twice: into the
;; options map passed to the belief path (:834) and into the tick's
;; :wm-version stamp beside :belief-model-manifest (arena-mode-flags,
;; :1045-1046). belief.clj only reads it (:keys with :or at :400-402, case
;; at :406) and writes it nowhere; its model-manifest (:286-293) stamps the
;; three hashes only. So the mode is not stamped by belief-model. Looked
;; for another writer: git grep of :likelihood-mode over futon2 src/ and
;; scripts/ at e1f6d909 finds only literal option maps in two bb scripts
;; (a_matrix_shadow.bb:65-66, aif/a_matrix_simulation.bb:199-225) and a
;; docstring in trace.clj:196 describing the :wm-version stamp, which
;; war_machine.clj builds. Found by conformance {:heuristic? true}.
{:spec/id :war-machine-belief-path-live
 :boxes
 [{:box/id :belief-model
   ;; model-manifest stamps the A/B/D content hashes (belief.clj:286-293);
   ;; the likelihood mode is an option it reads (:400-406)
   :site {:ns "futon2.aif.belief"}
   :writes [:observation-model-hash :transition-model-hash
            :initial-prior-hash]
   :reads [:likelihood-mode]}
  {:box/id :war-machine-report
   ;; the production seam decides the mode and writes it into the belief
   ;; options (:834) and the :wm-version stamp (:1045); hashes pass through
   ;; untyped
   :site {:file "scripts/futon2/report/war_machine.clj"}
   :writes [:likelihood-mode]}
  {:box/id :a-matrix-live-wiring-test
   ;; the paper-cited wiring evidence: reads all four stamps
   :site {:file "test/futon2/aif/a_matrix_live_wiring_test.clj"}
   :reads [:observation-model-hash :transition-model-hash
           :initial-prior-hash :likelihood-mode]}]}
